<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Bastarnae</h1><p class="st-meta">200 BCE – 280 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Probably Germanic people of the lower Danube and Carpathians who fought for Macedon against Rome and later joined the Goths.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Bastarnae appeared north of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> around 200 BCE, the first Germanic-speaking people known to Greek and Roman writers, though some ancient authors thought them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/celts">Celts</a>. One branch, the Peucini, lived on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peuce">Peuce</a> in the Danube delta.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were a warlike confederation of tribes, valued as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a>. Philip V and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus of Macedon</a> recruited them against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zarubintsy-culture">Zarubintsy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poienesti-lukashevka-culture">Poienești-Lukashevka</a> archaeological cultures are often linked to them. In 62 BCE they defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-antonius-hybrida">Gaius Antonius Hybrida</a> near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/histria">Histria</a>. In 29 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Marcus Licinius Crassus</a> defeated them and killed their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deldo">Deldo</a> in single combat.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the empire they remained a frontier people, joining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/carpi">Carpi</a> in 3rd-century raids. Around 280 the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/probus-emperor">Probus</a> settled a large number of Bastarnae in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, after which they disappear as a distinct people.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/bastarnae.jpg" alt="Bastarnae" width="320" height="272"><figcaption>Image: Terraflorin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dacia_125.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>200 BCE – 280 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Clondicus, Deldo</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Germanic (probably)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/moldova">Moldova</a>, <a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bastarni, Peucini</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=40&amp;focus=bastarnae" aria-label="Bastarnae on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5356 573 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bastarnae lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5676 829L5552 825M5676 829L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5552 825h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5676 829h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5676 829h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=40&amp;focus=bastarnae">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

